by welcoMattic at 2026-09-03T14:04:19Z

@nicolas-grekas thanks for the detailed direction. I pushed a series of commits on @imenezzine's branch (rebased on 8.2, Imen is co-author, we worked in pair-programming) that goes through every point of your comment. Here is what changed, point by point.

**Build on what is already there.** There is now a single HAR reader, `HarFile`, used by both `HarFileResponseFactory` (public API unchanged, it only gained an optional `MatcherInterface` argument) and `RecorderHttpClient`. The replay half is `MockHttpClient` fed by that reader. The recorder writes spec-compliant HAR: headers as `[{"name", "value"}]`, `creator.version` (from `InstalledVersions`), `time`, `timings`, `httpVersion`, `statusText`, `headersSize`, `bodySize`, `cookies`, and non UTF-8 bodies are stored with `"encoding": "base64"`. A record then replay round trip through the existing factory is covered by tests.

**Redaction on by default.** `DefaultRedactor` masks, before anything is written: headers (`Authorization`, `Proxy-Authorization`, `Cookie`, `Set-Cookie`, `DPoP`, `X-Api-Key`, `X-Auth-Token`), query string and form fields, and JSON fields of both request and response bodies. The lists follow the IANA OAuth parameters registry plus OIDC and SAML bindings: `access_token`, `refresh_token`, `id_token`, `code`, `client_secret`, `client_assertion`, `assertion`, `code_verifier`, `device_code`, `user_code`, `subject_token`, `actor_token`, `registration_access_token`, `auth_req_id`, `logout_token`, `SAMLRequest`, `SAMLResponse`, `SAMLart`, and common names like `password`, `secret`, `api_key`. URL fragments (implicit flow) and the `Location` header are redacted as URLs. The lists can be widened with `framework.http_client.recorder.redact.{headers,query,body}`, or the whole thing replaced by a `RedactorInterface` service (`framework.http_client.recorder.redactor`). Redaction is deterministic and applied on both sides, so replay keeps matching the live request.

**A miss in replay never reaches the network.** `#[UseRecord]` defaults to `RecorderMode::Replay` and a miss throws the dedicated `HarEntryNotFoundException` (a `TransportException`). Falling back to a real, recorded request is an explicit opt-in: `#[UseRecord(recordIfMissing: true)]`. The `REPLAY_AND_RECORD_IF_MISSING` mode is gone, and `RecorderMode` is now a real enum with cases (`Record`, `Replay`, `Passthrough`).

**`stream()` works.** Every mode returns an `AsyncResponse`. Recording happens in the chunk passthru and is flushed on the last chunk, so nothing is consumed eagerly and concurrent requests stay concurrent. Replayed responses share one `MockHttpClient` per recorder, so `stream([$r1, $r2])` works in replay mode too. Both are covered by tests.

**No process-wide state on the component.** `RecorderHttpClient` pulls its mode, HAR path and `recordIfMissing` flag from an injected `RecorderConfigurationInterface` on every request; the default `RecorderConfiguration` is immutable and `Passthrough`. The per-test state lives in the bridge only (`Symfony\Bridge\PhpUnit\HttpRecorder`, same model as `ClockMock`), driven by the subscriber before each test. FrameworkBundle injects it when the bridge is installed, and the recorder now decorates `http_client.transport` as the innermost decorator (like the mock transport) instead of every tagged client, so it sees absolute URLs after `ScopingHttpClient` and there is one recording per test for all clients. Requests are normalized through `HttpClientTrait::prepareRequest()` before being recorded, so `json`, array bodies, `query`, `auth_*` and `base_uri` are reflected in the file.

**Smaller ones.** The class-level `#[UseRecord]` is read (`forClassAndMethod()`, method level wins). `Kernel::VERSION` and `symfony/filesystem` are gone (native functions in `FilesystemStore`), and the bridge declares `symfony/http-client` in `require-dev` while staying PHP 8.1 compatible. `RecorderExtension` is replaced by a subscriber registered from `SymfonyExtension`, configured with the `http-recorder-directory` parameter. Tests were added for the component (recorder, redactor, matcher, factory), the bridge and the bundle wiring, and CHANGELOG entries moved to 8.2.

The PR description still needs a refresh (attribute namespace, defaults, a sample `.har`); we will take care of it.

