@nicolas-grekas all six are addressed in 96cc122, thanks for reprobing.

1. **Unconsumed responses.** The passthru skips `persist()` when `$context->getInfo('canceled')` is true, so nothing is written for a response destroyed unread, one where only `getStatusCode()` was called, or one that was explicitly canceled. I probed the neighbouring cases to make sure the guard is not too wide: a 404 or 500 consumed with `getContent(false)`, and a JSON error consumed with `toArray(false)`, are still recorded with their real status and body. The one case that now records nothing is an error status consumed through the thrown exception, since the body never reaches the passthru; that is the loud miss you asked for rather than an empty entry. It is documented on the class and in the PR description: to record an error path, consume it without throwing.

2. **`withOptions()`.** Implemented on the class like `NoPrivateNetworkHttpClient` does, merging into `$this->defaultOptions` with `mergeDefaultOptions()`. The clone also resets the replay client and its playback cursor. `->withOptions(['base_uri' => 'https://example.com'])->request('GET', '/rel')` now records `https://example.com/rel`, headers set that way are recorded, replay still matches, and the source client keeps its own defaults.

3. **`Record` truncation.** Moved to the bridge: the subscriber deletes the fixture at test start when the resolved mode is `Record`. The component only appends now, `$truncated` and `HarFile::clearEntries()` are gone, and two recorders created in the same test both write into the file (verified: two instances, two entries).

4. **Lock file.** It lives in the system temporary directory, named after a hash of the absolute fixture path, so nothing lands next to the records. I did not delete it after unlocking, since that races with a concurrent holder. Verified with four processes appending twenty entries each into one file: eighty entries, none lost, no stray lock.

5. **CHANGELOG.** Updated for sequential playback and for the matcher `HarFileResponseFactory` needs to read a recorder file. The PR description carries the same two notes plus the recording rule from point 1.

6. **Fabbot.** Fixed. For codespell I added `caf` to `ignore-words-list` in `.codespellrc` rather than applying the patch, so the test fixtures keep the real accented word.

