by nicolas-grekas at 2026-10-07T10:22:12Z

Thanks @imenezzine. I pushed a rework as a separate commit on top of yours:

- `MatcherInterface` is gone: requests match on method, URL and body once secrets are masked, so a field that changes on every request is ignored by adding it to `redact`. A matcher can come back later if needed, fed with the masked request.
- `RecorderMode` is now a string enum whose values are the ones of `SYMFONY_HTTP_RECORDER`: `replay`, `record`, `missing` and `passthrough`.
- `#[UseRecord]` paths are relative to the test file, or to the `http-recorder-directory` parameter when it is set (no more `@` prefix), and each data set gets its own file.
- `redact` is a single list, plus `redact_except`.

Also fixed: `record` deleted the file of a test that recorded nothing (a skipped one for example), and a miss printed the live URL with its secrets. Misses are now also reported as a PHPUnit warning, even when the tested code catches the exception. Recording an unchanged API again leaves the file as is, and multipart bodies match whatever their boundary.

